# Build context for S3TablesImage is this directory (agentcore-stack.ts passes
# `directory: path.join(mcpRoot, 's3_tables')`), so the sibling mcp/.dockerignore
# does NOT apply here — DockerImageAsset only reads the .dockerignore that sits
# in the context root. This file is that one.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs exactly two files: requirements.txt and
# agentcore_s3tables_mcp.py. Everything below is either not COPY'd or is
# generated locally, and a generated file in the context changes the asset hash
# on every synth — which is what kept this asset restaging.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.DS_Store
**/.venv
README.md
test_*.py
